### Count-down for-loop — negative demo
### This file INTENTIONALLY fails to compile.
### Build it to see the diagnostic the compiler produces when a
### for-loop with default step +1 would count 0 iterations because
### `from > to`. The old behavior was to silently skip the body —
### now it is a compile-time error directing you to `step -1`.
###
### Expected panic message from `ub build`:
###   for-loop: from (10) > to (1) with default step +1 loops 0 times
###     — use 'step -1' to count down

var i: int = 0

# Wrong: no explicit step. from > to. Compile-time error.
for i = 10 to 1
  print i
next i

# Correct alternatives (uncomment to compile successfully):
#
# for i = 10 to 1 step -1     # count down
#   print i
# next i
#
# for i = 1 to 10             # count up
#   print i
# next i

bye
